Do you know what you're talking about?

00:44:41.960 --> 00:44:43.860
Don't give me that innocent look.

00:44:44.990 --> 00:44:47.130
I haven't said two words to her since I come back.

00:44:48.360 --> 00:44:50.200
Because I sit here, you think I don't know what goes on?

00:44:50.970 --> 00:44:52.050
Not two words.

00:44:53.390 --> 00:44:54.230
I know plenty.

00:45:00.350 --> 00:45:02.370
Cut it out, will you, Sash? Cut it out.

00:45:03.500 --> 00:45:05.740
Take him down to that tramp if you want to make noise.

00:45:05.860 --> 00:45:07.240
Go on, take him down to her. Why don't you?

00:45:27.490 --> 00:45:29.970
Drive to right field. It's going...

00:45:30.090 --> 00:45:32.470
Going, it's gone! It's a home run!

00:45:32.750 --> 00:45:35.870
I got 12 cents to a beer. If I had 15, I'd be all right.

00:45:36.030 --> 00:45:38.030
I got, um, six cents here.

00:45:38.210 --> 00:45:38.530
Thanks.

00:45:39.790 --> 00:45:41.370
I ain't gonna stand up much longer.

00:45:42.050 --> 00:45:44.190
The heartache my old man gives me.

00:45:45.230 --> 00:45:46.790
You know what he likes to do most?

00:45:47.260 --> 00:45:49.100
Tear the dates off the calendar.

00:45:50.020 --> 00:45:53.140
Watching him, that's supposed to be my big Saturday night pleasure.

00:45:54.300 --> 00:45:55.880
Sometimes he loses all control.

00:45:56.080 --> 00:45:57.500
Tears off a whole week to once.

00:45:58.080 --> 00:45:59.500
Bleating like a billy goat.

00:46:00.120 --> 00:46:02.640
You know what would fill up that empty spot in your life?

00:46:03.340 --> 00:46:03.880
A door.

00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:06.320
Ask a sign of my customer.

00:46:06.620 --> 00:46:08.340
Frankie, that door guy got you.

00:46:08.460 --> 00:46:10.100
Makes a big difference in your life, don't it?

00:46:10.180 --> 00:46:10.540
Yeah, big.

00:46:13.670 --> 00:46:14.530
I want to see you.

00:46:15.930 --> 00:46:17.980
I want to see you.

00:46:18.750 --> 00:46:19.650
After the inning.

00:46:20.160 --> 00:46:21.540
I'll still bet you six to five.

00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:23.820
And it's a strike. Strike one.

00:46:27.770 --> 00:46:28.490
Getting started in.

00:46:29.130 --> 00:46:29.810
Fitch, London.

00:46:30.030 --> 00:46:36.000
swings and it's a high foul. Roberts is trying to get it. It may go into the stands. He's going to

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:42.860
try. It's going to be close. Roberts makes a tremendous leap and he's got it. You make out

00:46:42.860 --> 00:46:50.580
all right with the fellow at the job. Well the drumming job? Yeah fine. Well not so fine. He

00:46:50.580 --> 00:46:59.680
sort of topped out on me. He promised to call me but. Too bad. A million drummers in the world. How do I rate?

00:47:01.630 --> 00:47:04.260
Maybe he lost your number, happens.

00:47:05.670 --> 00:47:08.350
Maybe he's just wishing you'd get in touch.

00:47:10.580 --> 00:47:11.660
He'd think I was a pest.

00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:16.390
Chitty, good drummer. That's something. Don't turn up every day.

00:47:18.540 --> 00:47:19.700
Frankie, call.

00:47:39.020 --> 00:47:41.340
Come on, Molly. Watch the game, huh?

00:47:42.160 --> 00:47:46.200
Oh, I don't feel like a child. Why don't you go ahead? I'll wait for you.

00:47:53.190 --> 00:47:57.150
Yes, Studio B, Monday morning. Fine. Thank you, Mr. Lane. Bye.

00:48:00.190 --> 00:48:02.330
Monday. I got an audition Monday. Me.

00:48:02.710 --> 00:48:04.630
Yeah, he told me to join the union and be ready to work.

00:48:04.750 --> 00:48:05.670
Well, that's swell, Frankie.

00:48:05.890 --> 00:48:07.110
You know, he did lose my phone number.

00:48:07.310 --> 00:48:08.790
He'd been trying to find me all week long.

00:48:09.110 --> 00:48:10.490
Here, I was ready to forget the whole thing.

00:48:11.070 --> 00:48:12.810
Gee, if you hadn't opened your mouth, I wouldn't have called him.

00:48:13.070 --> 00:48:13.790
I'll show you what.

00:48:14.180 --> 00:48:15.820
I got an audition with a big band.

00:48:16.320 --> 00:48:17.220
Me, on TV.

00:48:17.750 --> 00:48:18.670
Practice a lot, Frankie.

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:21.380
Practice. I'll beat those heads to a shred.

00:48:22.290 --> 00:48:23.570
Only I gotta find a place where.

00:48:24.980 --> 00:48:26.160
Zosh can't stand the noise.

00:48:28.640 --> 00:48:28.920
Molly.

00:48:30.350 --> 00:48:34.840
I suppose maybe I could put the drums in your place and sort of drop in once in a while?

00:48:37.410 --> 00:48:40.060
Why not? Molly, why not?

00:48:43.520 --> 00:48:44.460
Johnny wouldn't understand.

00:48:45.950 --> 00:48:46.930
So what could he do?

00:48:48.970 --> 00:48:49.970
Tell him what he could do, Frankie.

00:48:52.070 --> 00:48:53.590
I look like Johnny can't do much about anything.

00:48:55.590 --> 00:48:56.590
Question what it does to him.

00:48:57.920 --> 00:48:59.040
I'm all he has in the world.

00:48:59.660 --> 00:48:59.980
Don't want to hurt you.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.840
Molly, for crying out loud.

00:49:03.260 --> 00:49:09.930
Oh, you don't know, Frankie. A fellow like him, times when we're alone.

00:49:10.800 --> 00:49:16.180
What does he do, cry? He's a lush, Molly. He's 100% habitual drunk.

00:49:17.130 --> 00:49:19.840
Everybody's habitual something. With him, it's liquor is out.

00:49:20.520 --> 00:49:22.370
Please, Molly. Molly-o.

00:49:23.010 --> 00:49:28.970
It ain't just that, Frankie. I don't want it to start with each other again.

00:49:30.510 --> 00:49:32.370
Look what you said about us not being good.

00:49:32.920 --> 00:49:33.680
It was the truth.

00:49:36.320 --> 00:49:38.580
Even before you went away, I tried to.

00:49:38.760 --> 00:49:42.510
It doesn't add up.

00:49:43.890 --> 00:49:44.390
It never did.

00:49:44.510 --> 00:49:45.050
It never can.

00:49:45.370 --> 00:49:46.290
Well, give it a chance.

00:49:46.490 --> 00:49:47.850
I told you it would one day.

00:49:49.700 --> 00:49:51.080
Oh, my life has been one day.

00:49:54.200 --> 00:49:55.100
On and on and on.

00:49:55.780 --> 00:49:56.540
I got drums.

00:49:56.680 --> 00:49:57.740
I'm headed for a good job.

00:49:58.320 --> 00:49:59.860
Is that so on and on and on?

00:50:00.570 --> 00:50:02.050
I make some money, make Zosh well.

